  "data_description_en": "Notes:\n1. All cases, Taiwanese and non-Taiwanese, matched to household registration in the NIIS database.\n2. The above vaccination data cover, since the start of COVID-19 vaccination, each dose, brand and vaccination\ndate of the vaccinated cases.\nExplanation of dose ordering and field definitions:\n(1) Ordered by the case's vaccination date, regardless of brand, excluding any later dose given less than 21 days after the previous dose.\n(2) If a case's primary booster and additional dose have the same vaccination date, brand and vaccination site, only the additional dose is listed.\n(3) Brand3 is only the primary booster.\n(4) The n in the provided Brand n is the maximum number of doses in the data provided in the current extraction.\nExample: if a case in the extraction range has a maximum of 13 CoV doses, the maximum dose provided for Brand is\nBrand13.\n3. Excludes the group who received a primary booster but fewer than 2 primary doses, or who did not receive an additional dose (note:\n(Note: this excluded group is limited to those who have never received an XBB-related vaccine.)\n4. Excludes cases whose household registration was removed or whose NIIS date of death is on or before 21 March 2021 (ROC 110/03/21) (inclusive)\n(Note: i.e. the vaccination date before COVID-19 vaccination was implemented.)",
  "notes_en": "Table (2) H_CDC_COVID19_2: the latest year available is 2022; 2023 has not yet been released.",
